### =============================================================================
### Task Tracker API - every endpoint, ready to run
###
### How to use: install the free "REST Client" extension in VS Code, open this file,
### and click "Send Request" above any request. Run them top to bottom the first time:
### later requests reuse values (token, ids) captured from earlier responses.
###
### Start the server first (npm start). For demo data run `npm run seed` once.
### =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. AUTHENTICATION
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register a new account  (user story 1)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dana Demo",
  "email": "dana@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Log in  (user story 2). Change the e-mail to alice@example.com after `npm run seed` for richer data.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dana@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### The token from the login response is reused by every request below
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. PROFILE  (user story 3)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### View my profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update my profile (any subset of name / jobTitle / bio; null clears jobTitle and bio)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dana Demo",
  "jobTitle": "Product Manager",
  "bio": "I like tidy backlogs."
}

### Change password (signs out every other session and returns a fresh token)
# PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/me/password
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "currentPassword": "Password123", "newPassword": "EvenBetter456" }


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. TEAMS AND INVITATIONS  (user story 11)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a team (I become its owner)
# @name createTeam
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Launch Squad",
  "description": "Everything for the October launch"
}

@teamId = {{createTeam.response.body.data.id}}

### List my teams
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Team details
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rename the team (owner or admin)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Launch Squad 2.0" }

### Invite someone by e-mail. The response contains the invitation `token` to share with them.
# @name invite
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "role": "member"
}

@inviteToken = {{invite.response.body.data.token}}
@inviteId = {{invite.response.body.data.id}}

### Pending invitations for the team (owner/admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoke an invitation
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/invites/{{inviteId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- The invitee's side: log in as bob (after `npm run seed`), then see and answer the invitation ---

# @name bobLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

@bobToken = {{bobLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### Invitations addressed to me
GET {{baseUrl}}/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### Accept (only the invited e-mail address can do this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/invites/{{inviteToken}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### Decline instead
# POST {{baseUrl}}/invites/{{inviteToken}}/decline
# Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### Team members
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Promote a member to admin (owner only). Replace 2 with the member's user id.
# PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/members/2
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "role": "admin" }

### Remove a member, or leave the team yourself (the owner cannot leave)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/members/2
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. TASKS  (user stories 4 - 9)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a personal task  (user story 4)
# @name createPersonal
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Write the launch checklist",
  "description": "Cover QA, comms and rollback.",
  "dueDate": "2026-11-15",
  "priority": "high"
}

@personalTaskId = {{createPersonal.response.body.data.id}}

### Create a team task and assign it to a teammate  (user stories 4 and 7)
# @name createTeamTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare press kit",
  "description": "Logos, screenshots and a one-pager.",
  "dueDate": "2026-11-01T17:30:00+05:30",
  "teamId": {{teamId}},
  "assigneeId": 2
}

@taskId = {{createTeamTask.response.body.data.id}}

### Create a task and let the AI draft the description  (user story 14)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Migrate billing to Stripe",
  "generateDescription": true
}

### One task
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tasks assigned to me  (user story 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?assignee=me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter by status  (user story 8). Several values allowed: open,in_progress
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?status=open,in_progress
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search title and description  (user story 9)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?q=press
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Combine everything: my open high-priority tasks, soonest due first, 10 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?assignee=me&status=open&priority=high&sortBy=dueDate&order=asc&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### What is overdue?
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?overdue=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Only personal tasks / only one team
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?teamId=personal
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?teamId={{teamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Partial update
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in_progress",
  "priority": "high"
}

### Assign (or reassign) to a teammate  (user story 7). Use { "assigneeId": null } to unassign.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/assignee
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigneeId": 2 }

### Mark as completed  (user story 6)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a task (creator, or team owner/admin)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{personalTaskId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. COMMENTS  (user story 10)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Add a comment
# @name comment
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Draft is ready for review." }

@commentId = {{comment.response.body.data.id}}

### List comments (oldest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Edit my comment (author only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Draft is ready for review - link in the thread." }

### Delete a comment (author, or team owner/admin)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments/{{commentId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. ATTACHMENTS  (user story 10)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Upload a file (multipart, field name must be "file")
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----TaskTrackerBoundary

------TaskTrackerBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

These are my meeting notes.
------TaskTrackerBoundary--

@attachmentId = {{upload.response.body.data.id}}

### List attachments
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Download
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/download
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete an attachment
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. NOTIFICATIONS  (user story 13)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Inbox (add ?unread=true to filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unread count
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark one as read
# PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/1/read
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark everything as read
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One-time ticket for browser EventSource clients (valid 30 s, single use)
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/stream-ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Live stream. The REST Client extension shows events as they arrive; assign a task to this user
### from another session and watch it appear. (From a terminal: curl -N <url> -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>")
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. GENERATIVE AI  (user story 14) - works offline with the built-in template provider
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Draft a description from a title
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/task-description
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Add dark mode to the dashboard",
  "context": "Users have asked for it in three support tickets."
}

### Summarise a task and its comments
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/tasks/{{taskId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. LOGOUT  (user story 12) and HEALTH
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Log out: this token stops working immediately (the next call with it returns 401 TOKEN_REVOKED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health check (no authentication)
GET http://localhost:3000/health
